[ ] Scope shared orientation to the querying worktree =orientation-worktree-context $Selected by coordination-selection (knowledge/decisions/coordination-selection-disposition.md, 2026-09-14) as the only work item justified by the pilot. Owner directive: no coordination machinery in code or guidance; the substrate is the shared intentions board, linked not built-in. Re-scoped 2026-09-15 after knowledge-pulse-kernel. (1) DONE: brief and full status/delta JSON now serve the worktree field (verified at 76bc22d). (2) REMAINING: the SessionStart wake is the kernel-rendered text summary (knowledge/specifications/wake-summary-contract.md, status --summary, 1000-byte budget), and checkpoints record no worktree identity, so a checkpoint label/note and since-then news recorded in worktree Y render as the last stop in a wake opened in worktree X (pilot run 1 control-arm finding). Claims are already worktree-relative. Scope the wake to the querying worktree within its budget, e.g. stamp checkpoints with the recording worktree and prefer or mark accordingly; amend the wake contract rather than bypass it; legacy identity-less checkpoints must not be presented as local; no workstream/session/declaration/handoff entities. Acceptance: a wake opened in a linked worktree on branch X does not present branch Y checkpoint or news as its own; wake budget and determinism tests still pass; cross-harness spot check in plot. Unblocks knowledge-pulse-dogfood and coordination-dogfood.$ !2 +implementation ^2026-09-14T18:22 #01a0a2a8-42cb-72d0-8af5-ed80b305bcca
